kind: Namespace
metadata:
  name: finalizer-lab
---
apiVersion: apiextensions.k8s.io/v1
kind: CustomResourceDefinition
metadata:
  name: dummydbs.storage.example.com
spec:
  group: storage.example.com
  names:
    kind: DummyDB
    plural: dummydbs
    singular: dummydb
  scope: Namespaced
  versions:
  - name: v1
    served: true
    storage: true
    schema:
      openAPIV3Schema:
        type: object
        properties:
          spec:
            type: object
            properties:
              size:
                type: string
Complete Solution
Step 1: Deploy the CRD and Namespace

Apply the CRD and wait a moment for it to register:

kubectl apply -f crd.yaml
sleep 3
Step 2: Deploy the Broken State

Apply the broken state:
```bash
kubectl apply -f broken-state.yaml
Step 3: Trigger the Trap and Rescue the CR
Attempt to delete the resource:

kubectl delete dummydb test-db -n finalizer-lab
Your terminal is now frozen. Press Ctrl+C to break out!

Now, clear the finalizer to allow the API server to complete the deletion:

kubectl patch dummydb test-db -n finalizer-lab -p '{"metadata":{"finalizers":[]}}' --type=merge

# Verify it is completely gone
kubectl get dummydb -n finalizer-lab
Step 4: Salvage the Orphaned Infrastructure

# Locate the orphaned volume
kubectl get pv

# Delete the orphaned volume to save cloud costs!
kubectl delete pv orphaned-data-pv